ought private  tracking scp-4910 brought its own  plethora of issues naturally or the  foundation would have secured it by now  the creature had some way of interfering  with recording devices rendering them  completely useless and of course that  meant that tirfing black had little to  no clue what the monster actually looked  like given that it disrupted any and all  recording equipment including cameras  and audio devices the task force's hands  were somewhat tied it forced alex and  his teammates to try and locate it  through more old-fashioned means  following up on eyewitness reports a lot  of which led them to a dead end every  now and then however one of these  sightings would prove to be genuine the  quickest way to tell was usually if a  person living near the place where a  report came in from had gone missing  lately civilians were  scp-4910's main source of food and a  recent disappearance in the area paired  with the sighting of something large and  four-legged usually meant that the beast  had come out of hiding to feed again  alright listen up team commanding  officer sawyer announced with the level  of militaristic speed and discipline  expected of them by the foundation alex  and the other members of the mobile task  force quickly filed out of the transport  and fell in ready and waiting to receive  their orders now you all know the reason  why we're here sawyer strode back and  forth arms behind his back as he  addressed what was left of his unit  three operatives not including himself  even so it is imperative you don't  forget it either so these are the facts  today the anomaly designated as  scp-4910 is still running wild but if we  have anything to say about it then that  sucker won't be running for much longer  the three troops gave a quick chant in  agreement although alex kept quiet just  mouthing along he wasn't exactly sure  that they would actually ever catch up  to the grinner so little footage of the  monster even existed meaning the team  still had little to no clue what this  thing was or if they were even equipped  to fight it and then again a huge part  of him didn't want to ever find scp-4910  knowing what it had done to the fallen  former members of mobile task force  epsilon so here's the latest commander  sawyer continued silencing the team  approximately 12 hours ago we received a  message from one of the foundation's  field operatives this agent has been in  deep cover living in a nearby town for a  number of years as he spoke the  commanding officer gestured down the  high ridge that they had landed on far  below sitting in the center of a huge  dip in the earth was a small township  there was barely enough room for more  than a few hundred people at most all  around this small urban center bordering  the entire town in an almost perfect  circle was a dense forest it was ideal  cover for the monster and alex could see  on his teammates faces that they all  knew it too with them in the town there  was no way they could cover every  possible avenue of approach this  operative is he the one that called in  the eyewitness report one of the team  warren piped up and asked that is  correct agent warren sawyer confirmed  that agent has agreed to meet us at a  rendezvous a few clicks north of here  the four of us will circumnavigate the  town stick to the cover of these woods  as we head out to make contact with him  from there he'll guide us to where the  creature was sighted the team gave  little response just a few low murmurs  expressing their collective apprehension  in a strange way alex found it  comforting that at the very least he  wasn't the only one having some serious  reservations about potentially coming  face to face with scp-4910  now boys  their commander's side  i get it all of us have been trying to  catch this freak for a long while and  we've lost a lot of good people from our  unit along the way but we are turfing  black you hear me you all know what that  name means tirfing as the sword from  norse mythology cursed to kill every  time it was drawn and that's us that is  exactly what we are gonna do when we  finally find this monster for all our  fallen brothers and sisters by the time  we're done with it the grinner will be  smiling out from the other side of its  ugly face now let's move out double time  with a half-hearted cheer the squad  prepared to start their hike through the  force that encircled the town the four  survivors of mobile task force epsilon  fanned out keeping close enough to see  and hear each other but not too close  that they were clustered together the  more they huddled up the easier it would  be to take them out if the grinner was  able to get the jump on them although he  should have been keeping his eyes  forward looking out for any tracks the  creature might have left alex couldn't  help checking over his shoulder the sun  was getting lower and lower in the sky  the day rapidly turning to night before  long their visibility would be  compromised severely limited by the lack  of natural light it was then he looked  to his fellow team members warren and  jones besides alex himself and the  squad's commander they were the only  turfing black operatives left warren had  always been the more brash and outspoken  of the group willing to stand up and  question the orders of commanding  officer sawyer alex could tell warren  was having the same worries about this  plan as he was the thick treeline gave  them plenty of cover but could also  easily work to the monster's advantage  allowing it to sneak up and get the drop  on the team with relative ease but both  alex and warren also knew that if the  mtf was pushed back towards the town  they would be trapped like fish in a  barrel just waiting to be picked off by  scp-4910  jones was walking slightly ahead of the  others his gaze rapidly scanning back  and forth across the forest before them  he was the team's most accomplished  tracker meaning he was always on the  lookout for anything that could give  them a better idea as to where the  grinner was heading or if it was nearby  from scratches on tree bark to series of  inhuman unnatural footprints belonging  to a large quadruped beast and of course  trails of blood or bodies if there was a  sign jones would find it much like alex  the other two operatives had become more  than a little jaded with their ongoing  hunt for the elusive entity but on top  of that not either one of them would  admit it to the others they were scared  of it too the things this creature were  capable of were enough to make anyone  think twice about wanting to find it as  much to quell his own fear and sorrow as  well as that of his teammates alex  started humming the tune to smile just  loud enough for them to hear but quiet  enough he hoped to not draw any unwanted  attention it was already dark by the  time tirfing black was beginning to  approach the coordinates where they had  arranged to meet the foundation agent  commander sawyer had given his troops a  silent hand signal and all of them had  lowered their night vision goggles  affixed to their helmets through the  fuzzy green hue of the optics jones was  the first to spot a figure leaning  against a tree waiting for them in the  distance  sir you whispered to sawyer catching his  attention and then making a gesture  towards the vaguely human shape in the  shadows ahead of them looking to where  jones had pointed alex and warren could  see the agent waiting for them following  their commander's lead they paced  steadily towards the undercover  operative it was only as they stepped  closer that they realized he wasn't  moving agent manning sawyer called out  to him trying to keep his voice as  hushed and low as possible no response  manning was still propped up against the  tree trunk the team were a few feet from  him now while the commander stepped up  to the agent and turned him around by  his shoulder only to recoil at what he  saw manning's eyes were open but  remained unblinking and lifeless but  that was far from the worst thing that  had happened to his face a huge  disproportionate grin had stretched his  mouth wider than was natural masses of  jagged uneven teeth had taken root  pushing from under his tongue and the  roof of his mouth filling his airways  with thick clusters of yellowy white  enamel there were so many new teeth  sprouting from manning's face that new  fixed and unsettling smiles had started  to form splitting open his cheeks back  back sawyer told his men in an urgent  hushed whisper remember boys we don't  know how contagious this thing is given  they had never seen it in the flesh that  was true  all previous failed attempts at bringing  in scp-4910 had ended with victims  displaying similar signs of some unknown  anomalous infection whatever it was it  seemed to have spread from the creature  itself causing human beings to  overproduce masses of teeth this started  with new clusters of dentins painfully  tearing through the mouth until the  victim could no longer speak or breathe  properly if given enough time the teeth  would begin forming elsewhere on the  body below the neck in places they  shouldn't be the lucky ones not that  there were many of them had managed to  get themselves medical attention soon  after they had been exposed within an  hour maybe two at best of an encounter  with scp-4910  there was still a chance of saving one  of its victims through intensive dental  surgery but three or four hours  afterward and it would already be too  late hearing the distant snap of a twig  jones turned with his weapon raised arms  locked in a combat ready stance possible  contact he declared aiming his gun into  the deep shadowy forest matching his  bearing and targeting the same area  sawyer gave a hand signal to alex and  warren urging them to lock and load  lifting their rifles they covered the  opposite direction just in case someone  or something came dashing out of 